    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d854">

                <pb facs="0990" n="878" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg878"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.6363/174: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-01-31T19:00:00+09:00">January 31, 1935—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 31—6:54 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. Department’s 10, January 30, 6 p.m.<anchor n="72" xml:id="d854-f1"/>
                    Conversations progressing steadily but no concrete results yet obtained.
                    Japanese officials promise definite written reply next week to memorandum
                    recently submitted by foreign oil companies containing their desiderata and it
                    is hoped then to be able to report specific results.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
